A||||1||ThatRickGuy||My Car Lost it Cool, and hmmm||||1||
Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||06-29-2001||09:52 PM||||Hey, what a day. Today was my going away luncheon, after 4 years of faithful service to the USMC I'm finally getting out. On my way home trying to get 8 miles south on I-95, I veared off on hwy 1 as 95 was a stand still. Thanks to this nasty heat wave, and a huge rush of drivers couppled w/ construction on I-95, my car lost it's cool. I knew it would happen, but my guage has never worked right (still havent found a short) but the idiot light popped on. I veared off into a parking lot, killed the engine, turned the defrost on full blast popped the trunk and hood, and after about 30 seconds it started puking coolant. grrrr. luckily it doesn't look like any thing was damaged, after a 2 hour cool down, 2 gallons of coolant and water, she started up fine and drove me home (north bound) with out a problem. <BR> As for the hmm, I was originally coming back to work because I left my cell phone here and I was expecting my new wheel bearing in today so I could work on it tonight. But I had to wait till 9pm so the traffic would be light enought for me to get through. Anyways, I got here and sure enough, there's the new bearing all wraped up and nice looking. I pulled it out of the box and noticed something. Here is a OEM replacement part for a car last produced 13 years ago, and it says "Patent Pending" on it... I just thought that was odd. Anyways, have fun.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-30-2001||12:57 AM||||Patent Pending?  That does seem odd to me.  I wonder how many other Fiero parts are patented by GM...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
